@@ -9258,3 +9258,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE D (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING; mandated; NEW mechanism) -- a game-AGNOSTIC ACTION-ROLE / object-interaction encoder for cross-game value transfer (ReactiveGWM, arXiv:2605.15256 VERIFIED). .400 (exp4331) found a LEARNED FRAME ENCODER yielded NO cross-game transfer (cross_game_state_reduction 1.008, CI95 [1.0,1.03], positive control passed) -- the 2nd cross-game-transfer null (after exp4318's generic features). DIAGNOSIS (ReactiveGWM): raw-frame features carry no game-invariant search-value signal; the fix is to DECOUPLE action-role / object-interaction structure from per-game pixels (a game-agnostic interaction representation that transfers zero-shot). Train the action-role encoder over the 11+ solved games' traces; re-test LEAVE-ONE-GAME-OUT cross-game value transfer for SEARCH EFFICIENCY (does a value head trained on the action-role features of the other games reduce search states on the held-out game?). HARD: report cross_game_state_reduction under leave-one-game-out + a positive control (baseline solves held-out). Emit learned_encoder_transfer_helps BARE bool := (state reduction > 1.0 AND CI95 lower bound > 1.0). verifier_is_oracle=false (the learned value head is oracle-distinct). retire_if_same_verdict: true -- a 3rd null across feature representations (generic, raw-frame, action-role) RETIRES the cross-game-transfer-for-search-efficiency direction. NO TRM training. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: action_role_encoder_transfer_no_improvement_positive_control_passed; results/experiment_4342_self_learning_action_role_cross_game_encoder.json
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE E (INFRA; SOTA-Ingestion Cycle) -- ingest the SOTA for the .402 headline open problem, conditioned on the .401 outcomes. Read research-studying.md / research-references.md filtered to the active tracks (in-generation moat settle + E3 ARC + cross-game self-learning) + run a FOCUSED fresh pass via the RELIABLE channel (scripts/sweep_clusters.py / sweep_semscholar.py + low-concurrency WebSearch/WebFetch of the top 5-8 papers -- NOT /deep-research, which is BANNED in-loop). CONDITIONAL on exp4338: if the in-generation moat REPLICATED (gate flipped) -> map the scale-up SOTA (adaptive guided generation, the next headline depth); if the moat RETIRED (corpus-specific) -> surface the consequence-based oracle-free verifier (arXiv:2602.06291 'Judging What We Cannot Solve', beats GenRM/LLM-judges where no oracle exists) as the LEAD .402 oracle-distinct candidate (a non-energy mechanism for the moat). Synthesize a SOTA->experiment mapping artifact (strongest 3-5 methods, each with a VERIFIED arXiv ID + a one-line .402 mapping + the failure mode). Update research-studying.md + FLAG the strongest method(s) for the .402 roadmap. Every method MUST carry a real, verifiable arXiv ID/URL (no citation = fabrication). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: sota_ingestion_v402_mapped; results/experiment_4343_sota_ingestion_v402.json
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE E (INFRA; Missing-Verifier Gap Logging) -- reconcile ops/verifier_registry.yaml + ops/verifier_gaps.md + ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml to the .401 truth, run the GAP-4 execution regression guard, and log the .401 missing-verifier gaps. Reconcile: the in-generation moat settle (exp4338 -- whether it replicated or retired; if retired, add the in-generation-moat scope to the exclusion manifest); the E3 ARC residual-mismatch gaps (exp4339/4340/4341 -- the missing-world-model-rule gaps as verifier gaps); the cross-game-transfer result (exp4342 -- if a 3rd null, retire the direction). Run the GAP-4 execution regression guard (the GAP-4 ARC execution win must not regress). Use the ROBUST aggregate-available-report-gaps helper (NO hard-block-all-False). Emit regression_guard_passed + registry_reconciled + manifest_reconciled + gaps_logged BARE. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: registry_gaps_manifest_reconciled_to_v401_truth_regression_guard_passed_True_gaps_logged_3; results/experiment_4344_verifier_registry_gaps_hygiene.json
+- 2026-06-17: PHASE E (INFRA; Hardware-Task Continuity, opportunistic per north-star §3) -- KV260 (THE sovereignty story; SSH-only, NEVER host SD-card) continuity check + an opportunistic GateMate/PolarFire reachability probe. north-star §3 relaxes the per-board mandate to KV260-until-terminal then opportunistic; this is the opportunistic check. PRECONDITION the KV260 via SSH-reachability (ssh -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o BatchMode=yes kria 'true'), NEVER a host-SD-card device-node check (the retired mechanism per the 2026-05-20 SSH-not-SD-card directive). If KV260 reachable: confirm the carnot_ising bitstream loads (xmutil listapps); record a board-state transcript. If unreachable: honest_verdict blocked_kv260_ssh_unreachable (NOT a fabrication). Opportunistic GateMate (openFPGALoader --detect) + PolarFire (ssh polarfire 'true') reachability. NO new FPGA-bitstream-redesign (re-scoped). DOC-ONLY/audit fallback keeps the boards visible if hardware is unreachable. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=complete: hardware_continuity_4345_kv260_kv260_xmutil_listapps_blocked_returncode_1_gatemate_blocked_gatemate_unreachable_polarfire_polarfire_ssh_reachable_ssh_only_opportunistic; results/experiment_4345_hardware_continuity.json
